---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import { docsImage } from "../lib/images";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="Mixing in key · Euphoria"
  description="How mixing in key works, why two keys mix, and how accurately Euphoria finds keys with its own neural network."
  route="/mixing"
  image="/og/mixing.png"
  imageAlt="Euphoria: mix in key. Six curves for the same key, a fifth, a fourth, the relative key, an energy boost and a clash."
  current="mixing"
  breadcrumb="Mixing in key"
>
<main id="top">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Mix in key.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Two tracks in compatible keys blend without clashing. Euphoria finds the key of every track, shows which ones mix, and lets you see and hear why.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section tone" id="wheel">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="rise">
        <h2>The Camelot wheel.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">DJs write keys as Camelot codes: a number from 1 to 12 and a letter, A for minor and B for major. Neighbours on the wheel mix. Euphoria shows every key both ways, 8A and A minor.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:20px;color:var(--soft);max-width:52ch">One step around the wheel is a perfect fifth. Two notes a fifth apart, played into an oscilloscope, draw a 3 to 2 curve. That curve is the Euphoria logo.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="wheel-figure rise"><img src={docsImage("keys-and-camelot/camelot-wheel.svg").src} alt="The Camelot wheel with minor keys inside and major keys outside, from 8A, A minor. The moves that mix in key are 7A and 9A, a fifth away, and 8B, the relative major. The bolder moves are 7B, the diagonal, 10A, the energy boost, 11B, the mood change, and 3A, the semitone boost."><figcaption>From 8A, A minor: the moves that mix, and the bolder ones.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="moves-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head rise">
        <h2>Every move, as a curve.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each move from 8A, drawn as the curve its two home notes trace. The names are the ones the app uses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="moves rise" id="moves">
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="1:1" data-loop data-offset="0.00" stroke-width="2.40" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 240)"></path></svg><b>Same key</b><span class="from">8A to 8A · 1 : 1</span><p>The same key. Always safe.</p><span class="tag mixes">Mixes in key</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="3:2" data-loop data-offset="0.35" stroke-width="2.40" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 270)"></path></svg><b>One step on the wheel</b><span class="from">8A to 9A · 3 : 2</span><p>A fifth apart. The classic harmonic mix.</p><span class="tag mixes">Mixes in key</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="4:3" data-loop data-offset="0.70" stroke-width="2.40" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 210)"></path></svg><b>One step on the wheel</b><span class="from">8A to 7A · 4 : 3</span><p>A fifth the other way: a fourth up.</p><span class="tag mixes">Mixes in key</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="6:5" data-loop data-offset="1.05" stroke-width="1.91" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 240)"></path></svg><b>Relative</b><span class="from">8A to 8B · 6 : 5</span><p>The other letter, the same number: the same notes in major.</p><span class="tag mixes">Mixes in key</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="8:5" data-loop data-offset="1.40" stroke-width="1.76" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 210)"></path></svg><b>Wheel diagonal</b><span class="from">8A to 7B · 8 : 5</span><p>One step and the other letter. Six of seven notes are shared, so the mood shifts while the blend holds.</p><span class="tag bold">Bolder move</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="9:8" data-loop data-offset="1.75" stroke-width="1.54" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 300)"></path></svg><b>Energy boost</b><span class="from">8A to 10A · 9 : 8</span><p>Two numbers up. The key rises by a whole tone, a clear lift.</p><span class="tag bold">Bolder move</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="1:1" data-loop data-offset="2.10" stroke-width="2.40" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 330)"></path></svg><b>Mood change</b><span class="from">8A to 11B · 1 : 1</span><p>The same home note in the other mode, A minor to A major. A dramatic change of mood.</p><span class="tag bold">Bolder move</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="16:15" data-loop data-offset="2.45" stroke-width="1.14" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 90)"></path></svg><b>Semitone boost</b><span class="from">8A to 3A · 16 : 15</span><p>Seven numbers up. The key rises by a semitone, a dramatic lift whose melodies clash.</p><span class="tag bold">Bolder move</span></div>
        <div class="move"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="45:32" data-loop data-offset="2.80" stroke-width="0.72" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 60)"></path></svg><b>A clash</b><span class="from">8A to 2A · 45 : 32</span><p>Keys a tritone apart share little, so Euphoria never suggests this.</p><span class="tag clash">Clashes</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tone" id="mixing">
    <div class="wrap mixer">
      <div class="rise">
        <h2>Try any two keys.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">Two notes played into an oscilloscope draw a curve. Keys that mix draw simple ones. Pick a key for this track and the next, and watch.</p>
        <div class="pickers">
          <div class="picker">
            <div class="picker-head"><b>This track</b><span id="this-name">8A · A minor</span></div>
            <div class="keys" id="this-keys"></div>
            <div class="mode" role="group" aria-label="This track: minor or major" id="this-mode"><button type="button" data-letter="A" aria-pressed="true">Minor (A)</button><button type="button" data-letter="B" aria-pressed="false">Major (B)</button></div>
          </div>
          <div class="picker">
            <div class="picker-head"><b>Next track</b><span id="next-name">9A · E minor</span></div>
            <div class="keys" id="next-keys"></div>
            <div class="mode" role="group" aria-label="Next track: minor or major" id="next-mode"><button type="button" data-letter="A" aria-pressed="true">Minor (A)</button><button type="button" data-letter="B" aria-pressed="false">Major (B)</button></div>
          </div>
          <div class="presets" aria-label="Common moves">
            <button type="button" data-move="1">One step up</button><button type="button" data-move="-1">One step down</button><button type="button" data-move="relative">Relative key</button><button type="button" data-move="diagonal">Wheel diagonal</button><button type="button" data-move="2">Energy boost</button><button type="button" data-move="mood">Mood change</button><button type="button" data-move="7">Semitone boost</button><button type="button" data-move="6">A clash</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="scope rise" aria-live="polite">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" id="mix-ghost" stroke-width="0.4" style="opacity:.18"></path><path class="mark-path" id="mix-curve" data-curve="3:2" data-intro stroke-width="1.4"></path></svg>
        <div class="verdict" id="verdict">Mixes well.</div>
        <div class="verdict-sub" id="verdict-sub">One step on the wheel. A minor to E minor is a perfect fifth, 3 : 2.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="accuracy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="model rise" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="model-text">
          <h2>Our own key model.</h2>
          <p class="lede">Euphoria detects keys with drone-v2, a neural network trained by the Euphoria project and built into the app. It runs on your computer in plain Rust, with no GPU and nothing to download.</p>
          <p class="model-claim"><b>15% more tracks with the exact key</b> than KeyFinder, the free key detector that Mixxx also builds in.</p>
          <p class="model-note">Measured on the 604 GiantSteps Key previews of electronic dance music. GiantSteps guided drone-v2's development, so this is not a blind test. <a href="https://github.com/lvndry/euphoria/blob/main/docs/concepts/accuracy.md">Every result, including the misses</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bars" role="img" aria-label="Exact key on 604 GiantSteps previews: Euphoria 69.9 percent, Essentia 61.3 percent, KeyFinder 60.6 percent. MIREX score, which also gives part credit to near misses: Euphoria 75.4, Essentia 69.5, KeyFinder 69.4.">
          <div class="bars-head"><span>Exact key, on 604 dance tracks</span><span>Score</span></div>
          <div class="bar-row is-ours"><span class="bar-name">Euphoria<small>drone-v2, our own neural network</small></span><span class="bar-track"><i style="--value:69.9"></i></span><b class="num">69.9%</b><b class="num mirex">75.4</b></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-name">Essentia<small>The open-source audio analysis toolkit from the Music Technology Group in Barcelona, on its best key setting</small></span><span class="bar-track"><i style="--value:61.3"></i></span><b class="num">61.3%</b><b class="num mirex">69.5</b></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-name">KeyFinder<small>The free key detection app, also built into Mixxx DJ</small></span><span class="bar-track"><i style="--value:60.6"></i></span><b class="num">60.6%</b><b class="num mirex">69.4</b></div>
          <div class="bars-foot"><span>0%</span><span>50%</span><span>100%</span></div>
          <p class="bars-more">Score is the standard MIREX score, which also gives part credit to near misses that still mix, such as a key a fifth away. When Euphoria misses, its runner-up is often right: the key or its runner-up is right for 80.8% of tracks.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tone" id="tools">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head rise">
        <h2>Mixing in key, in the app.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The same rules run everywhere you look for the next track.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tools rise" id="tools-list">
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#library")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="3:2" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 240)"></path></svg></span><span><b>Mixes well with</b><span>Beside every track in the inspector: the tracks that mix after it, ranked by key move, tempo and energy.</span></span></a>
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#palette")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="3:1" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 60)"></path></svg></span><span><b>Search by key</b><span>Type 8A in the command palette for 8A first, then one step and relative, marked as pills.</span></span></a>
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#decks")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="1:1" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 180)"></path></svg></span><span><b>Next on deck B</b><span>With a track on deck A, the decks list what mixes well after it. Choose which moves count.</span></span></a>
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#focus")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="4:3" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 150)"></path></svg></span><span><b>Plan a transition</b><span>Pick the next track in the focus view and get the window, the bars and the key relation in a sentence.</span></span></a>
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#set")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="5:3" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 270)"></path></svg></span><span><b>Sets in key</b><span>The set builder orders tracks along an energy curve with every mix in a compatible key.</span></span></a>
        <a class="tool" href={withBase("/features#set")}><span class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="5:4" data-static stroke-width="3.4" style="color:oklch(0.58 0.15 330)"></path></svg></span><span><b>The key path of a playlist</b><span>Above a playlist, each key in play order, with a red mark on any step that does not mix.</span></span></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="shot-frame rise" style="margin:48px 0 0"><img src={docsImage("desktop-app/focus-view.png").src} alt="The focus view in the app: the track's sections, waveform with cues, energy and stem lanes, the two tracks it mixes into with their key relation, and the Plan card describing the transition in a sentence." width="1600" height="968" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px"><figcaption style="margin-top:14px;color:var(--soft);font-size:15px">The focus view: the tracks this one mixes into, with the key relation of each, and the plan for the transition.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="wrap closing-grid">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" id="closing-mark" aria-hidden="true"><path class="mark-path" data-curve="3:2" data-intro data-on-view stroke-width="2"></path></svg>
      <div class="rise">
        <h2>Play it in key.</h2>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/lvndry/euphoria/releases/latest/download/Euphoria.dmg">Download for macOS</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href={withBase("/#install")}>Install on Linux</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
